WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.500
Webhooks. Send signed HTTPS events to your own systems when tasks and comments change.

2
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:09.500
Use it for: chat alerts; data sync.

3
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:15.000
A task or comment changes → Flow signs the event → POST to your endpoint → Retried if it fails

4
00:00:15.800 --> 00:00:21.730
(Note: The endpoint is a local test receiver, which only this isolated test server allows; real servers accept public HTTPS addresses.) Add the URL that should receive events…

5
00:00:21.730 --> 00:00:25.220
…and add it.

6
00:00:25.220 --> 00:00:30.180
The signing secret is shown once (blurred here). Copy it now.

7
00:00:30.180 --> 00:00:34.940
Send a test to check the receiver…

8
00:00:34.940 --> 00:00:42.390
…every delivery is logged, with Redeliver.

9
00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:48.390
The URL is refused: It must be public HTTPS; localhost and private networks aren't allowed. The webhook turned itself off: It failed 15 times in a row or returned 410. Fix the receiver and switch it back on.

10
00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:52.890
HMAC-SHA256 signatures
